- It's too much tea in this episode,

00:28:49.630 --> 00:28:50.600
the tea's being spilled.

00:28:50.600 --> 00:28:51.640
Okay, but what are you,

00:28:51.640 --> 00:28:54.000
as someone who actually
works in the industry,

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:55.670
what do you feel about that argument,

00:28:55.670 --> 00:28:56.819
of like the, "I buy anime merch,

00:28:56.819 --> 00:28:59.180
so therefore I have the right
to pirate," kinda thing?

00:28:59.180 --> 00:29:01.365
- I mean, you can't use it as a reason

00:29:01.365 --> 00:29:05.490
because I think, I don't
know how to explain this.

00:29:05.490 --> 00:29:08.540
Like, for example, royalties for goods,

00:29:08.540 --> 00:29:11.443
so I've heard from friends in the industry

00:29:11.443 --> 00:29:13.980
that they go to different departments.

00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:17.963
It's not always directly
to that specific creator.

00:29:19.635 --> 00:29:20.939
- So, what are you saying?

00:29:20.939 --> 00:29:22.770
If they buy merch,

00:29:22.770 --> 00:29:25.510
the money still doesn't go
back to the original creator?

00:29:25.510 --> 00:29:28.190
- It does, it depends, I think,
on the contract they had,

00:29:28.190 --> 00:29:30.309
so I've heard
- Okay.

00:29:30.309 --> 00:29:31.567
- I'm not in that department.

00:29:31.567 --> 00:29:34.680
- I imagine the bigger
of a brand the anime is,

00:29:34.680 --> 00:29:36.200
the easier it is to get a better deal

00:29:36.200 --> 00:29:38.819
in terms of royalties
and costs, I imagine.

00:29:38.819 --> 00:29:40.640
- Yeah.
- I don't know.

00:29:40.640 --> 00:29:43.830
- Yeah 'cause one thing
that always confuses me

00:29:43.830 --> 00:29:45.480
is that people think that,

00:29:45.480 --> 00:29:49.350
I know there's lots of
arguments that have been made

00:29:49.350 --> 00:29:51.550
that doing X worth is better

00:29:51.550 --> 00:29:53.880
for supporting the industry than doing Y,

00:29:53.880 --> 00:29:56.120
and I dunno how much, like,

00:29:56.120 --> 00:29:57.980
I don't know where they're
getting this information from,

00:29:57.980 --> 00:30:00.490
'cause none of these people
are working in the industry.

00:30:00.490 --> 00:30:03.655
So every argument I see
on both sides of things

00:30:03.655 --> 00:30:05.950
a lot of the times just anecdotal-

00:30:05.950 --> 00:30:07.850
- It's just speculation.
- and speculation.

00:30:07.850 --> 00:30:09.269
- There's no theory behind it.

00:30:09.269 --> 00:30:12.630
They're just like, Oh, I
feel good buying merch.

00:30:12.630 --> 00:30:15.200
It feels like if I buy official merch,

00:30:15.200 --> 00:30:17.670
because it's tied to that particular IP,

00:30:17.670 --> 00:30:20.671
you just feel like, Oh, I'm supporting it,

00:30:20.671 --> 00:30:22.520
I'm helping to spread the love,

00:30:22.520 --> 00:30:24.910
I'm putting money into
something that's official.

00:30:24.910 --> 00:30:26.093
So therefore in the back of their head,

00:30:26.093 --> 00:30:28.180
they're just like, yeah, that's
gonna go back to the creator

00:30:28.180 --> 00:30:29.013
in some way, right?

00:30:29.013 --> 00:30:29.955
Like they own it.
- I mean, it's better

00:30:29.955 --> 00:30:31.500
than not doing anything.

00:30:31.500 --> 00:30:32.333
- Of course,

00:30:32.333 --> 00:30:34.510
but is it the best way to
support that particular creator

00:30:34.510 --> 00:30:35.343
of the IP?

00:30:35.343 --> 00:30:36.176
No.
- Not the best,

00:30:36.176 --> 00:30:37.227
but better than nothing.

00:30:37.227 --> 00:30:40.310
- So the best wages, legally streaming?

00:30:40.310 --> 00:30:41.160
Paying for the services?

00:30:41.160 --> 00:30:43.800
Is that the best way in your opinion?

00:30:43.800 --> 00:30:47.270
- I've heard that the DVDs,
Blu-ray DVDs for example,

00:30:47.270 --> 00:30:49.240
in Japan, I'm not sure about the U.S,

00:30:49.240 --> 00:30:52.620
but in Japan, buying the
Blu-ray DVDs is the best.

00:30:52.620 --> 00:30:54.317
That's when they know like-

00:30:54.317 --> 00:30:56.230
- Yeah, 'cause they measure success

00:30:56.230 --> 00:30:57.360
from Blu-ray sales, right?

00:30:57.360 --> 00:31:01.920
- Yeah, that and like the
original sources sale-

00:31:01.920 --> 00:31:04.328
- Yeah, like the manga
and stuff like that,

00:31:04.328 --> 00:31:05.890
I've heard that.
- That's what I've heard.

00:31:05.890 --> 00:31:07.390
- 'Cause I always try to
make sure I buy my manga

00:31:07.390 --> 00:31:08.460
firsthand now.

00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:09.883
Like, even if it's an older series

00:31:09.883 --> 00:31:12.250
where I can easily go to
a bulk offer or something

00:31:12.250 --> 00:31:13.410
and buy it for 100 Yen,

00:31:13.410 --> 00:31:15.440
I always just try and go to the bookstore,

00:31:15.440 --> 00:31:16.273
the first-hand book store.

00:31:16.273 --> 00:31:19.300
'Cause I've heard that
is truly the best way

00:31:19.300 --> 00:31:20.850
to support the creator, right?

00:31:20.850 --> 00:31:23.010
- I guess 'cause when it's pre-owned-

00:31:23.010 --> 00:31:23.951
- The royalties don't go.

00:31:23.951 --> 00:31:26.100
- 'Cause I mean like 2/3 of my JoJo merch

00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:27.440
is pre-owned stuff.

00:31:27.440 --> 00:31:29.117
- That's because it's like-
- You can't get that stuff

00:31:29.117 --> 00:31:30.970
anymore, 'cause for some reason-

00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:33.913
- It wasn't made for you, it
wasn't available at the time.

00:31:35.220 --> 00:31:36.053
You don't deserve it. (laughing)

00:31:36.053 --> 00:31:37.883
- I deserve all the JoJo merch.

00:31:39.020 --> 00:31:41.433
I spent thousands of dollars
on like Yahoo auction,

00:31:41.433 --> 00:31:42.725
but none of that goes to...

00:31:42.725 --> 00:31:44.553
Because a lot of the time as well,

00:31:44.553 --> 00:31:46.960
like this merch is like
what, like 100 bucks?

00:31:46.960 --> 00:31:48.450
And then two years later on Yahoo auction

00:31:48.450 --> 00:31:51.010
it's 300 bucks and someone
made a nice profit.

00:31:51.010 --> 00:31:51.990
I mean good for them.

00:31:51.990 --> 00:31:54.010
- Araki's definitely not seen that profit.

00:31:54.010 --> 00:31:57.320
- I mean, anything that
I've bought that's brand new

00:31:57.320 --> 00:32:00.250
is probably the Jump store
stuff that we both bought,

00:32:00.250 --> 00:32:03.910
'cause the JoJo exhibition
museum was canceled

00:32:03.910 --> 00:32:05.680
and normally you have to
go to the JoJo exhibition

00:32:05.680 --> 00:32:06.660
to get the stuff,

00:32:06.660 --> 00:32:08.500
but they were like, "Hey, you
can just order it online."

00:32:08.500 --> 00:32:09.910
So I ordered like-
- You got the suits.

00:32:09.910 --> 00:32:11.060
- The suits as well I got,

00:32:11.060 --> 00:32:13.280
but the thing is, with the suits,

00:32:13.280 --> 00:32:16.830
that's Bandai collaboration
with Perfect Suit Factory.

00:32:16.830 --> 00:32:19.800
So there's like two companies
that are making this thing

00:32:19.800 --> 00:32:22.277
before it gets to the-
- They're taking most of it.

00:32:22.277 --> 00:32:23.900
- So, like these $500 suits,

00:32:23.900 --> 00:32:26.800
how many of that goes to Shonen Jump

00:32:26.800 --> 00:32:28.020
and then, are like..

00:32:28.020 --> 00:32:30.180
Like the animators aren't
seeing that shit, right?

00:32:30.180 --> 00:32:31.960
The animators are still underpaid as fuck.

00:32:31.960 --> 00:32:33.850
- I mean, I don't think
there's anything we can do for-

00:32:33.850 --> 00:32:36.340
- Well, they're underpaid
because it's just Japan's salary,

00:32:36.340 --> 00:32:37.803
the average salary in Japan-

00:32:38.650 --> 00:32:39.483
- Mike!

00:32:40.370 --> 00:32:41.960
- Man, Mike is taking a beating.

00:32:41.960 --> 00:32:44.222
- The average salary in general is low.

00:32:44.222 --> 00:32:45.550
- (Joey and Gigguk) Yeah.

00:32:45.550 --> 00:32:47.240
- I mean, I feel like with animators,

00:32:47.240 --> 00:32:50.350
it's a systematic problem
with how the industry works

00:32:50.350 --> 00:32:51.186
as a whole.

00:32:51.186 --> 00:32:52.636
- That's a whole other can of worms.

00:32:52.636 --> 00:32:54.280
- That's a whole other can of worms.

00:32:54.280 --> 00:32:56.840
- That's also just like Japanese culture.

00:32:56.840 --> 00:32:59.560
- Yeah, that's a whole
different argument to be had.

00:32:59.560 --> 00:33:02.660
But I think one thing I see

00:33:02.660 --> 00:33:05.010
with a lot of like Western
Twitter and Western people

00:33:05.010 --> 00:33:08.700
is that I feel like they don't
want to support the industry,

00:33:08.700 --> 00:33:10.462
mostly because they're not happy with

00:33:10.462 --> 00:33:12.310
some of these bigger companies

00:33:12.310 --> 00:33:15.161
or the image of like say
Crunchyroll or Funimation

00:33:15.161 --> 00:33:18.100
and it's less of, "I don't
wanna support the industry,"

00:33:18.100 --> 00:33:20.910
and more of, "I don't wanna
support these companies

00:33:20.910 --> 00:33:21.800
in particular.

00:33:21.800 --> 00:33:23.413
- Yeah, you don't wanna
support the companies

00:33:23.413 --> 00:33:26.060
that are representing the
industry in our country, right?

00:33:26.060 --> 00:33:27.266
- I can understand it at times

00:33:27.266 --> 00:33:29.720
'cause there's a lot of
arguments that people make

00:33:29.720 --> 00:33:32.510
like underpaying translators
that comes up a lot,

00:33:32.510 --> 00:33:34.250
and you know, like last year,

00:33:34.250 --> 00:33:36.580
it was voice actor of Funimation.

00:33:36.580 --> 00:33:37.500
Like, there's a lot of reasons

00:33:37.500 --> 00:33:38.910
why people might not want to, right?

00:33:38.910 --> 00:33:41.408
It's tough, 'cause it's-

00:33:41.408 --> 00:33:45.950
- Because I don't think there's
a right or wrong argument

00:33:45.950 --> 00:33:48.250
but what I feel sometimes is that

00:33:48.250 --> 00:33:49.650
a lot of people won't
support the industry,

00:33:49.650 --> 00:33:52.390
unless there's like a perfect system

00:33:52.390 --> 00:33:55.520
where all the money they go
to goes to this one creator.

00:33:55.520 --> 00:33:57.809
They wanna-
- Utopian system?

00:33:57.809 --> 00:34:00.130
- Yeah, like a utopian system

00:34:00.130 --> 00:34:02.930
where every creator has a
fucking Patreon or something

00:34:02.930 --> 00:34:05.280
and they can support any creator they want

00:34:05.280 --> 00:34:06.220
and how much they want,

00:34:06.220 --> 00:34:09.070
and that's just not a business
model, you know what I mean?

00:34:09.070 --> 00:34:11.710
And I feel like a lot of
people use that justification

00:34:11.710 --> 00:34:13.790
to say, "Hey we're not
supporting the creator

00:34:13.790 --> 00:34:15.658
how I want to support the creator.

00:34:15.658 --> 00:34:18.070
So I'm just not gonna support anything."

00:34:18.070 --> 00:34:21.487
And I feel like there must be
a better way to go about it

00:34:21.487 --> 00:34:23.703
than that because there's never
gonna be a perfect system.

00:34:23.703 --> 00:34:25.960
- I mean, Trigger kinda
did the right thing, right?

00:34:25.960 --> 00:34:26.793
They have a Patreon,

00:34:26.793 --> 00:34:27.710
they have a Twitch stream
where they do like-

00:34:27.710 --> 00:34:29.360
- How much does their
Patreon get at the moment?

00:34:29.360 --> 00:34:31.690
- I'm not too sure, but-
- I think I checked,

00:34:31.690 --> 00:34:34.030
and I was like, that is
nowhere near enough to-

00:34:34.030 --> 00:34:35.360
- Oh no, definitely not.

00:34:35.360 --> 00:34:37.337
It's basically just like
a side revenue for them.

00:34:37.337 --> 00:34:38.810
But at least it's a way

00:34:38.810 --> 00:34:42.960
that will actually go
directly to the studio,

00:34:42.960 --> 00:34:46.050
and is a payment method or donation method

00:34:46.050 --> 00:34:48.533
that Westerners are very
familiar with, right?

00:34:48.533 --> 00:34:50.190
- It's good to have just an option

00:34:50.190 --> 00:34:51.380
to do something like that.

00:34:51.380 --> 00:34:53.560
It's like, Hey, do you wanna
directly support the studio?

00:34:53.560 --> 00:34:55.697
And like, you know-
- I think Pixie has that.

00:34:55.697 --> 00:34:57.530
It's not a studio, but like
there are some illustrators.

00:34:57.530 --> 00:35:00.127
- Oh, yeah, Pixie kinda has
that as well, definitely.

00:35:00.127 --> 00:35:04.050
But I mean, that's really the only thing

00:35:04.050 --> 00:35:07.030
and barely anybody's utilizing it.

00:35:07.030 --> 00:35:10.330
I've never heard of a
manga artist using Patreon.

00:35:10.330 --> 00:35:13.280
- Is it like a pride thing in Japan?

00:35:13.280 --> 00:35:15.070
Like not wanting to ask people for money?

00:35:15.070 --> 00:35:17.200
'Cause like begging is
really like not a thing here.

00:35:17.200 --> 00:35:18.570
- I don't know.

00:35:18.570 --> 00:35:20.770
- I mean, culturally
begging is not a thing,

00:35:21.626 --> 00:35:22.690
not even for homeless people.

00:35:22.690 --> 00:35:25.654
- Yeah, homeless people just
do their own thing like that.

00:35:25.654 --> 00:35:28.110
- It's true, I've never seen
a homeless person begging.

00:35:28.110 --> 00:35:29.550
- 'Cause it's really disrespectful, right?

00:35:29.550 --> 00:35:31.680
- Yeah, it's not a thing here.

00:35:31.680 --> 00:35:33.530
Even the homeless here are respectful

00:35:33.530 --> 00:35:35.970
where they're just like, "No,
no, no, keep your money."

00:35:35.970 --> 00:35:38.387
- Like, "I'm homeless,
I still have my pride."

00:35:40.009 --> 00:35:42.090
- I think it's just a
different culture altogether.

00:35:42.090 --> 00:35:43.802
- There's a lot of it that
comes down to that there

00:35:43.802 --> 00:35:47.300
I think in the industry and
how people want it to change.

00:35:47.300 --> 00:35:48.356
It's just not going to.

00:35:48.356 --> 00:35:50.800
- I also think a really
big root of the problem,

00:35:50.800 --> 00:35:52.740
when it comes to at
least the anime industry

00:35:52.740 --> 00:35:56.820
is that they truly, even
though in my experience,

00:35:56.820 --> 00:35:59.200
having done stuff with a
lot of different studios

00:35:59.200 --> 00:36:01.310
and productions and whatnot in anime,

00:36:01.310 --> 00:36:03.770
they're aware of the Western industry,

00:36:03.770 --> 00:36:05.570
they just don't really
give a shit about them.

00:36:05.570 --> 00:36:07.410
- I would say they care a lot,

00:36:07.410 --> 00:36:08.943
they just don't know what to do.

00:36:08.943 --> 00:36:10.240
- It's not their first priority though.

00:36:10.240 --> 00:36:13.487
The first priority is always
the Japanese market, right?

00:36:13.487 --> 00:36:15.330
And that's how they measure their success.

00:36:15.330 --> 00:36:18.110
I mean, of course I'm sure
all of these studios now,

00:36:18.110 --> 00:36:19.103
it's 2020, right?

00:36:19.103 --> 00:36:20.990
Like I think most of them are aware now

00:36:20.990 --> 00:36:23.270
that there are way more Western fans

00:36:23.270 --> 00:36:24.500
who are into their anime

00:36:24.500 --> 00:36:26.933
than there will ever be
Japanese fans, right?

00:36:26.933 --> 00:36:27.860
But-
- I mean, in China alone-

00:36:27.860 --> 00:36:30.779
- Or just Southeast Asia.

00:36:30.779 --> 00:36:33.170
- All the mobile games
coming out of China.

00:36:33.170 --> 00:36:34.670
- Even if you just look at Southeast Asia,

00:36:34.670 --> 00:36:35.965
that's more people just in general

00:36:35.965 --> 00:36:38.020
who will watch the anime
and enjoy the anime

00:36:38.020 --> 00:36:39.850
and be willing to spend the money on it.

00:36:39.850 --> 00:36:43.020
But because the Japanese
anime industry is,

00:36:43.020 --> 00:36:44.125
a lot of it is so old fashioned,

00:36:44.125 --> 00:36:47.797
and thinking just locally,
that they just like,

00:36:47.797 --> 00:36:50.640
"Okay, we understand that
there are all these people

00:36:50.640 --> 00:36:53.560
out here who are probably
willing to pay for our stuff,

00:36:53.560 --> 00:36:55.060
we just don't know how to do it.

00:36:55.060 --> 00:36:57.230
We can't be bothered to
figure out how to do it."

00:36:57.230 --> 00:36:59.040
- Japanese culture in
general though, isn't it?

00:36:59.040 --> 00:37:01.160
- Yeah, it's just like, for example,

00:37:01.160 --> 00:37:03.770
the DVD and Blu-ray business model

00:37:03.770 --> 00:37:05.840
is just not going to work abroad,

00:37:05.840 --> 00:37:06.870
you know what I mean?

00:37:06.870 --> 00:37:08.607
I mean, it can prop up the
anime industry here in Japan

00:37:08.607 --> 00:37:10.830
and it has for the longest time,

00:37:10.830 --> 00:37:12.960
but it took them like how
many years to figure out

00:37:12.960 --> 00:37:14.852
that people just don't
wanna buy DVDs and Blu-ray?

00:37:14.852 --> 00:37:15.917
- That's like if Crunchyroll was like,

00:37:15.917 --> 00:37:17.740
"We're gonna open up a
blockbuster tomorrow,

00:37:17.740 --> 00:37:20.000
come on in and rent your DVDs."

00:37:20.000 --> 00:37:24.380
It's just like, no, it's not...(laughing)

00:37:24.380 --> 00:37:27.370
It's shocking how many people in Japan

00:37:27.370 --> 00:37:29.630
do not know streaming services.

00:37:29.630 --> 00:37:31.730
Like even young people are just not aware.

00:37:31.730 --> 00:37:35.030
They're like, "Oh, you can
watch anime on Netflix?"

00:37:35.030 --> 00:37:39.863
- They usually record it on
their TV when it's playing live.

00:37:39.863 --> 00:37:41.610
- but it's like, I'm not
staying up until 3:00 AM

00:37:41.610 --> 00:37:43.230
to watch a fucking run.

00:37:43.230 --> 00:37:46.253
- I've never seen a place
where they sell CRT TV so much.

00:37:50.200 --> 00:37:52.336
Smash players were like, "Yes, yes,"

00:37:52.336 --> 00:37:53.367
but everyone else is like,

00:37:53.367 --> 00:37:55.824
"Why the fuck would I need a CRT TV?

00:37:55.824 --> 00:37:56.834
There's so many.

00:37:56.834 --> 00:37:57.955
- I don't even know what a CRT TV is.

00:37:57.955 --> 00:37:58.980
- Those big fucking chunky ones,

00:37:58.980 --> 00:38:00.900
the static-
- The big TVs.

00:38:00.900 --> 00:38:01.750
- I see so many of them for sale-

00:38:01.750 --> 00:38:04.040
- The TV that you grew
up with, like the giant,

00:38:04.040 --> 00:38:05.450
like the brick of a TV.

00:38:05.450 --> 00:38:06.910
- Ow, thick.
- The thick boys, yeah.

00:38:06.910 --> 00:38:07.850
- I was in Akihabara,

00:38:07.850 --> 00:38:09.360
and there was like a
brand new electronic store

00:38:09.360 --> 00:38:11.715
there was like LCD, like thin TVs,

00:38:11.715 --> 00:38:14.400
and there's a whole section for CRT TVs.

00:38:14.400 --> 00:38:17.130
And I'm like, who the fuck is buying this?

00:38:17.130 --> 00:38:19.630
Genuinely, who the fuck
is buying CRT TV set,

00:38:19.630 --> 00:38:21.180
except for Smash players?

00:38:21.180 --> 00:38:25.650
- But like the secondhand
store here in Japan

00:38:25.650 --> 00:38:27.470
is fuckin' on another level,

00:38:27.470 --> 00:38:29.280
because you go into a secondhand store

00:38:29.280 --> 00:38:31.660
and they have like fucking laser discs

00:38:31.660 --> 00:38:34.820
in pristine condition.
- Perfect condition.

00:38:34.820 --> 00:38:38.180
- I bought a fuckin'
like full LaserDisc set

00:38:38.180 --> 00:38:41.270
of all the episodes of
"Evangelion" for like 500 Yen.

