us the villains of anime

01:21:31.401 --> 01:21:32.993
if anything, right.

01:21:32.993 --> 01:21:34.230
- Some people would probably,

01:21:34.230 --> 01:21:37.980
who are in the middle of nowhere
that have no anime friends

01:21:37.980 --> 01:21:39.866
and they're getting bullied for it,

01:21:39.866 --> 01:21:41.394
and they're like, "Oh
these people like anime

01:21:41.394 --> 01:21:42.380
and they're actually cool?"

01:21:42.380 --> 01:21:45.591
- Yeah, punch 'em back.
- Anime is not a lame thing?

01:21:45.591 --> 01:21:47.160
Yes, you're cool.

01:21:47.160 --> 01:21:49.300
- All I remember was, I was suited up,

01:21:49.300 --> 01:21:50.170
Sydney was suited up

01:21:50.170 --> 01:21:53.440
and then Joey walks up in fuckin'...

01:21:53.440 --> 01:21:54.273
I can't remember what you were wearing.

01:21:54.273 --> 01:21:59.063
- I was in a JoJo shirt, and like shorts.

01:22:00.502 --> 01:22:03.680
And I looked at Gigguk,
like so properly dressed

01:22:03.680 --> 01:22:05.390
with like collar, shirt and everything.

01:22:05.390 --> 01:22:07.170
Sydney was in like this really nice dress,

01:22:07.170 --> 01:22:10.450
and I'm just there with like
my jeans and fucking sneakers,

01:22:10.450 --> 01:22:13.603
and I'm just like, "Ss'up,
hero of anime right here."

01:22:14.944 --> 01:22:16.240
- I took that to another party as well.

01:22:16.240 --> 01:22:18.560
- This is like, "Oh my God,
that's how YouTubers dress?"

01:22:18.560 --> 01:22:22.700
That's like, you know...

01:22:22.700 --> 01:22:24.470
Celebrity wear.
- Celebrity wear?

01:22:24.470 --> 01:22:26.583
- Celebrities wear like jumpsuits.

01:22:28.990 --> 01:22:31.350
- I'm so celebrity, I
wear Uniqlo everywhere.

01:22:31.350 --> 01:22:35.140
- Yeah, I don't think
that anyone understood

01:22:35.140 --> 01:22:36.720
what I actually said in my speech.

01:22:36.720 --> 01:22:39.804
You're the only one who
anyone could understand.

01:22:39.804 --> 01:22:40.959
- I was told no one could hear me.

01:22:40.959 --> 01:22:41.792
- A lot of them did speak English though.

01:22:41.792 --> 01:22:43.530
- Because you started speaking

01:22:43.530 --> 01:22:45.470
and the speakers just weren't on.

01:22:45.470 --> 01:22:49.133
All we could see was-
(Joey laughing)

01:22:50.933 --> 01:22:53.130
- It's an amazing speech,
it such a good speech.

01:22:53.130 --> 01:22:54.690
- What was more hilarious

01:22:54.690 --> 01:22:57.390
was just not only just
Connor's speakers not being on,

01:22:57.390 --> 01:22:59.833
but just 50 Japanese business men,

01:22:59.833 --> 01:23:02.400
just like really seriously
just looking down at the iPad,

01:23:02.400 --> 01:23:03.516
just being like...

01:23:03.516 --> 01:23:05.804
- They were paying attention.

01:23:05.804 --> 01:23:07.800
- You have to bear in mind as
well, I can't see anything.

01:23:07.800 --> 01:23:10.830
Like I'm just talking to a
webcam, I don't see shit.

01:23:10.830 --> 01:23:12.020
So as far as I know,

01:23:12.020 --> 01:23:13.923
like I'm just talking in
the fucking void over here,

01:23:13.923 --> 01:23:16.323
with my shitty Japanese,
(speaking in Japanese).

01:23:20.164 --> 01:23:22.100
Oh my God.
- That was really funny.

01:23:22.100 --> 01:23:25.320
- But no, that was like a
really interesting experience

01:23:25.320 --> 01:23:27.610
for me 'cause that was
like a holy shit moment.

01:23:27.610 --> 01:23:29.400
Have I made it? Is this the point?

01:23:29.400 --> 01:23:31.970
- We met some really
fuckin' cool people there.

01:23:31.970 --> 01:23:36.390
- Who was like, the person you
met that stood out the most?

01:23:36.390 --> 01:23:38.640
Or which company did
you like freak out over?

01:23:41.590 --> 01:23:44.970
- Obviously like the Shonen
Jump guys were there,

01:23:44.970 --> 01:23:47.090
but I think the coolest one,

01:23:47.090 --> 01:23:49.150
just because it just kinda
came out of nowhere was,

01:23:49.150 --> 01:23:51.440
I think I was talking to
the Shonen Jump people,

01:23:51.440 --> 01:23:53.590
and they were like,
what manga do you like?

01:23:54.534 --> 01:23:55.730
What are you interested in?

01:23:55.730 --> 01:23:57.600
Obviously I laid out a
bunch of Shonen Jump stuff

01:23:57.600 --> 01:23:58.547
and then one of the guys was like,

01:23:58.547 --> 01:24:00.640
"Oh, what about stuff
that's not Shonen Jump,

01:24:00.640 --> 01:24:02.150
like I'm just genuinely curious."

01:24:02.150 --> 01:24:04.170
And I think I said "Berserk"

01:24:04.170 --> 01:24:05.450
because I fucking love "Berserk".

01:24:05.450 --> 01:24:07.450
And then literally the moment
after I said "Berserk",

01:24:07.450 --> 01:24:08.700
some guy tapped me on the shoulder

01:24:08.700 --> 01:24:11.100
almost like, "Hi, I'm
the publisher 'Berserk'."

01:24:12.138 --> 01:24:14.477
I was like, (gasping)
- The editor.

01:24:14.477 --> 01:24:16.010
- Was things like dusty?

01:24:16.010 --> 01:24:17.710
He's like, "I've never done that."

01:24:17.710 --> 01:24:19.970
I've been hired for five years
and I haven't done anything.

01:24:19.970 --> 01:24:24.420
- I've never even met Miura
in my life. (laughing)

01:24:24.420 --> 01:24:26.640
So, he said that and I read the card.

01:24:26.640 --> 01:24:27.473
I'm like, Oh shit, yeah,

01:24:27.473 --> 01:24:29.180
that is like the publication of "Berserk".

01:24:29.180 --> 01:24:31.800
And I just said, like, "Not to be rude,

01:24:31.800 --> 01:24:33.483
what the fuck is Miura doing?

01:24:33.483 --> 01:24:34.578
What is he doing?"

01:24:34.578 --> 01:24:37.140
- What's going on?
- What's going on with that?

01:24:37.140 --> 01:24:38.716
- Let's jump right into it.

01:24:38.716 --> 01:24:41.103
- Like, "You're his publisher right?

01:24:41.980 --> 01:24:44.550
Just give me the details,
what's he doing?"

01:24:44.550 --> 01:24:46.100
And he's like, "Oh no, he's
working hard, don't worry."

01:24:46.100 --> 01:24:48.680
I'm like, "Yeah, that's what
they all say." (laughing)

01:24:48.680 --> 01:24:52.610
- Idol master in the
background, "I'm working hard."

01:24:52.610 --> 01:24:53.760
- Are you winning, son?

01:24:55.655 --> 01:24:56.730
- Yeah, but that was really cool,

01:24:56.730 --> 01:24:58.900
Danny Choo was really cool-
- Danny Choo was really cool.

01:24:58.900 --> 01:25:01.520
- because I think it's safe to say

01:25:01.520 --> 01:25:03.590
that Danny Choo she is one of those people

01:25:03.590 --> 01:25:08.590
who really put anime weeb
culture in the West on the map.

01:25:08.920 --> 01:25:11.550
Because I think it's not
too much of a stretch

01:25:11.550 --> 01:25:13.800
to say that without
Danny Choo's influence,

01:25:13.800 --> 01:25:16.290
I don't think any of us would
really even be interested

01:25:16.290 --> 01:25:18.860
in Japanese culture,
especially people on the West.

01:25:18.860 --> 01:25:22.700
- He did so much for,
not only like our culture

01:25:22.700 --> 01:25:23.580
but our industry as well.

01:25:23.580 --> 01:25:26.600
'Cause he was one of the first
foreigners who moved to Japan

01:25:26.600 --> 01:25:28.370
and really put a highlight
on a lot of things

01:25:28.370 --> 01:25:29.203
going on in the Japanese industry.

01:25:29.203 --> 01:25:30.970
- He had to blog about it.
- Yeah, exactly,

01:25:30.970 --> 01:25:32.830
'cause before, I remember it was just like

01:25:32.830 --> 01:25:34.700
Japan was just kind of a black hole.

01:25:34.700 --> 01:25:37.470
Nobody knew shit that
was happening in Japan,

01:25:37.470 --> 01:25:39.100
we just got anime somehow.

01:25:39.100 --> 01:25:43.080
But he actually spotlighted
a lot of the things going on,

01:25:43.080 --> 01:25:44.419
and if not for him,

01:25:44.419 --> 01:25:46.208
I probably wouldn't even
have even considered moving

01:25:46.208 --> 01:25:50.201
to Japan or have any interest
in the industry itself.

01:25:50.201 --> 01:25:52.520
- He did some great motivational speeches

01:25:52.520 --> 01:25:55.300
at a lot of events like anime expo.

01:25:55.300 --> 01:25:56.807
- And he's a really down
to earth guy as well.

01:25:56.807 --> 01:25:59.580
- He's so humble, incredibly
incredibly humble.

01:25:59.580 --> 01:26:01.640
- Everything he's done,
he's like so humble

01:26:01.640 --> 01:26:02.473
and so down to earth.

01:26:02.473 --> 01:26:03.840
- He just showed up with his doll.

01:26:03.840 --> 01:26:05.470
- Yeah, he showed up with this smart doll,

01:26:05.470 --> 01:26:08.064
yeah, that was so cool,
shout out to Danny Choo.

01:26:08.064 --> 01:26:11.450
But you should have been
there bro. (laughing)

01:26:11.450 --> 01:26:12.330
- I'm pissed off I missed out.

01:26:12.330 --> 01:26:15.300
- How was the Crunchyroll
anime awards compared to that?

01:26:15.300 --> 01:26:17.830
(Joey and Gigguk laughing)

01:26:17.830 --> 01:26:20.100
- I mean, one day I
came back into my room,

01:26:20.100 --> 01:26:23.540
and there was a trash bag full
of stuff that wasn't mine.

01:26:23.540 --> 01:26:24.445
Can you believe that?

01:26:24.445 --> 01:26:25.890
- In your hotel?
- In my hotel room.

01:26:25.890 --> 01:26:27.015
- Who went in there?

01:26:27.015 --> 01:26:27.848
- I don't know.

01:26:27.848 --> 01:26:28.830
I called them up and I'm like,

01:26:28.830 --> 01:26:32.460
Hey, there's a, just a giant
bag of trash in my room.

01:26:32.460 --> 01:26:33.293
What's up with that?

01:26:33.293 --> 01:26:34.230
And they're like, "Really?"

01:26:34.230 --> 01:26:35.736
They didn't believe me.

01:26:35.736 --> 01:26:36.890
I'm like, come, come.

01:26:36.890 --> 01:26:38.490
- The maids probably cleaned up.

01:26:38.490 --> 01:26:40.140
- Well I think what they did
is the maids were cleaning

01:26:40.140 --> 01:26:42.290
and they just forgot the
bag, so I didn't care much.

01:26:42.290 --> 01:26:43.907
They gave me a letter that was like,

01:26:43.907 --> 01:26:46.450
"Dear CDawg, sorry that we
left trash in your room."

01:26:46.450 --> 01:26:48.703
And I was like, why is it CDawg?

01:26:49.687 --> 01:26:51.040
- Probably the name that
they put on the reservation?

01:26:51.040 --> 01:26:51.960
- No, it was Connor,

01:26:51.960 --> 01:26:54.550
'cause I checked in with
my real name and I know,

01:26:54.550 --> 01:26:57.000
the guy must have known or
something, it was weird as fuck.

01:26:57.000 --> 01:26:58.720
